ll Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL mock draft: Reid's midseason first-round predictions for all 32 picks","description":"Which NFL team could land Drew Mestemaker? Who needs Chris Cole, Ashton Hampton or Jamari Johnson? Jordan Reid projected first-round picks for 2027 -- and a trade.","published":"2026-11-18T15:09:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50502243/2027-nfl-mock-draft-reid-midseason-32-first-round-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft: Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets, Chargers in race for No. 1 pick","description":"Five NFL teams have at least 5% odds to land the No. 1 pick in 2027, per ESPN's Football Power Index: the Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets and Chargers.","published":"2026-11-18T13:32:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50510863/2027-nfl-draft-top-pick-dolphins-titans-eagles-jets-chargers","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation, Jordan Reid and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Anger Index: Why Texas Tech, Tennessee and the Group of 6 should be mad","description":"Ranking the teams who should be most upset about their latest CFP ranking.","published":"2026-11-18T04:25:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510905/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-texas-tech","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4905925/devan-thompkins","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devan_Thompkins"},"pick":{"pick":32,"round":1,"team":"BUF","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Devan Thompkins","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devan_Thompkins","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-18T13:13:47Z","intro":"Devan Thompkins is an American college football defensive tackle for the Alabama Crimson Tide. He previously played for the USC Trojans.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Thompkins attended St. Mary's High School in Stockton, California for three years before transferring to Edison High School in Stockton for his senior year. He played basketball at St. Mary's and did not play football until his senior year at Edison. He played defensive end and tight end in high school and had nine tackles and caught three passes for 24 yards. Thompkins committed to the University of Southern California (USC) to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Thompkins played in three combined games his first two years at USC in 2022 and 2023. In 2024, he started six of 13 games and recorded 24 tackles and 1.5 sacks. In 2025, he had 31 tackles and three sacks. After the season, Thompkins entered the transfer portal."}]}}